    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4458" root="ثعلب" body-key="v">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرْضٌ مُثَعْلِبَةٌ</span></b>  <i>A land having</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَعَالِب</span> [or <i>foxes</i>]:
(S:) or, <i>having many thereof;</i> as also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَرضٌ مَثْعَلَةٌ</span>;
(K;) which is from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثُعَالَةٌ</span>; or it may be from
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ثَعْلَبٌ</span>, like <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَعْقَرَةٌ</span> applied to “ a land having many
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَقَارِب</span> [or scorpions]. ” (S, L.)

